Pre:    "Enable MLD snooping" -- on by default on the DUT and on IE520-sa (confirmed below).

VERDICT: PASS -- both VLANs receive the group once each, with no leaking and no HSL error.

STEP 1 -- "Have 2 clients in different vlans join same multicast group" -> "no leaking
          between vlans", and no "HSL: ERROR: Error Adding ... multicast entry" message
  eth1 (vlan20) and eth2 (vlan1) both join ff1e::1:300; 20 frames from fd32:b1f0:dff8:d703::1
      eth1 20/20, eth2 20/20 -- exactly one copy each (a leak or double-forward would show >20)
      show ipv6 mroute ff1e::1:300:  in vlan30, out vlan1 + vlan20
      show log | include HSL|Error Adding|Failed to add:  no matches (only the command's own
      IMISH echo)

STEP 2 -- "show ipv6 mld snooping statistics interface" -> "mld member groups are registered
          on each VLAN"
      vlan1:  ff1e::1:300  Interface vlan1 (sa3)         Exclude  Last reporter fe80::86e3:27ff:fe87:780
      vlan20: ff1e::1:300  Interface vlan20 (port3.0.13) Exclude  Last reporter fe80::3f84:db77:9294:e805

STEP 3 -- "Registered router port to each VLAN, transmit MLD report" -> "MLD report forwarded
          to router port"
  The DUT IS the router here, so its own "show ipv6 mld snooping mrouter" is empty. The
  snooping switch with a router port is IE520-sa: eth2's report reached the DUT from the SA
  (vlan1's last reporter is the SA's link-local), i.e. the SA forwarded it out its router port.
      IE520-sa show ipv6 mld snooping mrouter (same session, 15:08 NZST):
        VLAN 1   sa3   Dynamically Learned
      i.e. the SA learned its uplink to the DUT as the router port, and eth2's report went out it.
